<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law (Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation))",
        "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law faithfully reproduces Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation) morphology" ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py, docs/media/runions_leaf_venation_growth.gif, runions_leaf_venation_metrics.csv implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 40.9/100, audit 2026-10-18-venation-audit) and the assessments." ;
    schema:about "Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: In v1, specimen photographs are not yet segmented into vascular graphs, closed-mode anastomosis lacks persistent source tagging and planarity checks, and loop nesting runs on a synthetic 8x8 lattice rather than the simulated/segmented dual faces",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Open Ginkgo biloba and closed dicot space-colonization simulators, Horton-Strahler ordering and pipe-model radius propagation, and loop nesting CDF plots",
        "reported_in_source: Katifori & Magnasco (2012) and Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) quantify hierarchical areole loop nesting via recursive minimum-width vein removal on the planar dual graph",
        "reported_in_source: Murray (1926) derives minimum-work pipe scaling r_parent^3 = sum r_child^3, while Price et al. (2013) measure 349 cleared leaves (1,514,771 junctions) showing a transition from Murray's law in minor veins (gamma ~ 3, area ratio ~ 1.25) to area-preserving branching in major veins (gamma ~ 2, area ratio ~ 1.01)",
        "reported_in_source: Runions et al. (2005) define open auxin space-colonization (Eq. 1) via Voronoi nearest-vein neighborhoods and closed reticulate venation (Eq. 2-3) via Toussaint Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) neighborhoods with tagged-source anastomosis",
        "transfer_boundary: Comparison of simulated vascular hierarchies and segmented specimen networks against Price et al. (2013) and Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015)" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/docs/media/runions_leaf_venation_growth.gif, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/runions_leaf_venation_metrics.csv; output: runions_leaf_venation_comparison.png; organism: Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/c89d18d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 9b9080151e73e5b8bf2e2b214040b93303d1faaea0b8391fd0aa193cc0743686; artifact_sha256: 79a46c05f0cf7c61e8021754a50e88c48d4288c7a4c5704b5a4aae36343fb1c5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/venation/ginkgo_open_venation_specimen.jpg=5a620943881fe698..., datasets/venation/reticulate_vein_skeleton_specimen.jpg=6d06d3e545bd585b..., datasets/venation/venation_reference.json=4edb5b774f01935b...}; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Runions et al. (2005) define open auxin space-colonization (Eq. 1) via Voronoi nearest-vein neighborhoods and closed reticulate venation (Eq. 2-3) via Toussaint Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) neighborhoods with tagged-source anastomosis | Murray (1926) derives minimum-work pipe scaling r_parent^3 = sum r_child^3, while Price et al. (2013) measure 349 cleared leaves (1,514,771 junctions) showing a transition from Murray's law in minor veins (gamma ~ 3, area ratio ~ 1.25) to area-preserving branching in major veins (gamma ~ 2, area ratio ~ 1.01) | Katifori & Magnasco (2012) and Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) quantify hierarchical areole loop nesting via recursive minimum-width vein removal on the planar dual graph; reconstructed_in_script: Open Ginkgo biloba and closed dicot space-colonization simulators, Horton-Strahler ordering and pipe-model radius propagation, and loop nesting CDF plots; transfer_boundary: Comparison of simulated vascular hierarchies and segmented specimen networks against Price et al. (2013) and Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015); does_not_claim: In v1, specimen photographs are not yet segmented into vascular graphs, closed-mode anastomosis lacks persistent source tagging and planarity checks, and loop nesting runs on a synthetic 8x8 lattice rather than the simulated/segmented dual faces]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.12.3.207>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1004680>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0037994>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0085420> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-6> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Mathematical Morphogenesis Model" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 4.09e-01 .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Validated Mathematics of Biological Form" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law — Code-to-model traceability: 62/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Functions and Lean 4 theorems are cited in docstrings, but Lean Section 13 defines murray_root_capacity and murray_tip_sum identically and compute_murray_radii_and_strahler() has a 3-tuple return type annotation while returning a 4-tuple. Evidence: morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean L365–L413: Section 13 Lean definitions and theorems in v1 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L365-L413>; 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py L397–L461: Return annotation mismatch in compute_murray_radii_and_strahler() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py#L397-L461>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law — Model fidelity to source: 45/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Open space-colonization (Eq. 1) grows a valid dichotomous Ginkgo tree, but closed reticulate venation (L329-340) fuses new tips to any node within 1.32*d_k except the immediate parent rather than implementing Runions et al. (2005) Sec. 4 persistent V(s) source tagging, producing 571 degenerate triangles and 375 crossing edge pairs. Evidence: 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py L279–L344: Open Eq. 1 vs shortcut closed fusion without source tagging or planarity check <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py#L279-L344>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law — Morphometric validation: 30/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "In v1, simulate_hierarchical_strahler_tree() samples directly from the JSON gamma_k column and correlates against the same JSON medians (circular r=0.9956), and compute_katifori_loop_nesting() runs on a synthetic 8x8 lattice rather than the simulated or segmented venation graph. Evidence: 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py L518–L560: Circular sampling in simulate_hierarchical_strahler_tree() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py#L518-L560>; 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py L566–L649: Synthetic 8x8 grid in compute_katifori_loop_nesting() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py#L566-L649>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): open Ginkgo venation anastomosing cycle count L = E - V + 1 = 0 loops (reference 0, Runions et al. 2005 ACM Trans. Graph. 24(3):702-711 Sec. 3 (open venation tree)) [Euler-Poincaré independent cycle rank E - V + 1 on open Voronoi space-colonization tree]; Murray's cube law root-to-tip conservation ratio r_root^3 / (N_tips * r_tip^3) = 1.0 ratio (reference 1.0, Murray 1926 PNAS 12:207 / Runions et al. 2005 Sec. 3.5 / Lean 4 theorem murray_1926_tree_conservation) [ratio of petiole root cubic radius r_root^3 to sum of terminal veinlet cubic radii sum r_tip^3] — r_root^3 = 397.0, N_tips = 397; open venation binary junction median daughter/parent area ratio (A_1 + A_2)/A_0 = 1.2223 area ratio (reference 1.2599, Murray 1926 symmetric bifurcation 2^{1/3} = 1.2599 / Price et al. 2013 PLoS ONE e85420 Fig. 3) [median (r_1^2 + r_2^2) / r_0^2 across binary bifurcations of the grown open venation tree]; closed reticulate venation anastomosing loop count L = E - V + 1 = 902 areole loops (reference 150, Runions et al. 2005 ACM Trans. Graph. 24(3):702-711 Sec. 4 Eq. (2)-(3)) [Euler cycle rank E - V + 1 of closed Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) space-colonization network] — V = 1056, E = 1957; Horton-Strahler order 1 vs order 8 median area-ratio shift = 0.2489 delta area ratio (reference 0.24, Price, Knox & Brodribb 2013 PLoS ONE 8(12):e85420 Fig. 4 (order 1 median 1.25 -> order 8 median 1.01)) [decrease in median daughter/parent cross-sectional area ratio from terminal minor veins (order 1) to major midveins (order 8)] — Pearson r across Strahler orders = 0.9956; Katifori & Magnasco (2012) unweighted hierarchical loop nesting number i_u = 0.8234 nesting index i_u (reference 0.68, Katifori & Magnasco 2012 PLoS ONE e37994 / Ronellenfitsch et al. 2015 PLoS Comput. Biol. e1004680 Fig. 3b) [mean subtree partition balance q_j = 1 - |r_j - s_j|/(r_j + s_j - 1) under iterative minimum-width vein removal] — high-noise / additive control i_u = 0.6155." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-6> ;
    pk:hasProbability 3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law — MorphoEval overall 40.9/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Initial v1 implementation of Runions et al. (2005) leaf venation space colonization, Murray (1926) / Price et al. (2013) vascular scaling, and Katifori & Magnasco (2012) loop nesting. Independent audit by Claude Sonnet 5.5 High scored v1 at 41.6 overall, identifying five concrete defects (unsegmented specimen images, triangle short-circuiting in closed anastomosis, synthetic 8x8 Katifori grid, circular Strahler sampling, and vacuous Lean 4 definitions) targeted for Step 12 remediation. Overall 40.9/100 (faithfulness 32.1, reproducibility 61.2); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit c89d18d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 45, Morphological realism / specimen match 20, Parameter expressivity 40, Morphometric validation 30, Source and data traceability 68, Code-to-model traceability 62, Reproducibility package 55. Output judged: runions_leaf_venation_comparison.png: rendered output of 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py at c89d18d, image/png, 1136399 B, 2475×1530 px, artifact_sha256 79a46c05f0cf7c61e8021754a50e88c48d4288c7a4c5704b5a4aae36343fb1c5 (sha256 79a46c05f0cf7c61e8021754a50e88c48d4288c7a4c5704b5a4aae36343fb1c5), spec_fingerprint 9b9080151e73e5b8bf2e2b214040b93303d1faaea0b8391fd0aa193cc0743686. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 9b9080151e73e5b8bf2e2b214040b93303d1faaea0b8391fd0aa193cc0743686; artifact_sha256: 79a46c05f0cf7c61e8021754a50e88c48d4288c7a4c5704b5a4aae36343fb1c5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/venation/ginkgo_open_venation_specimen.jpg=5a620943881fe698..., datasets/venation/reticulate_vein_skeleton_specimen.jpg=6d06d3e545bd585b..., datasets/venation/venation_reference.json=4edb5b774f01935b...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Runions et al. (2005) define open auxin space-colonization (Eq. 1) via Voronoi nearest-vein neighborhoods and closed reticulate venation (Eq. 2-3) via Toussaint Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) neighborhoods with tagged-source anastomosis | Murray (1926) derives minimum-work pipe scaling r_parent^3 = sum r_child^3, while Price et al. (2013) measure 349 cleared leaves (1,514,771 junctions) showing a transition from Murray's law in minor veins (gamma ~ 3, area ratio ~ 1.25) to area-preserving branching in major veins (gamma ~ 2, area ratio ~ 1.01) | Katifori & Magnasco (2012) and Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) quantify hierarchical areole loop nesting via recursive minimum-width vein removal on the planar dual graph; reconstructed_in_script: Open Ginkgo biloba and closed dicot space-colonization simulators, Horton-Strahler ordering and pipe-model radius propagation, and loop nesting CDF plots; transfer_boundary: Comparison of simulated vascular hierarchies and segmented specimen networks against Price et al. (2013) and Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015); does_not_claim: In v1, specimen photographs are not yet segmented into vascular graphs, closed-mode anastomosis lacks persistent source tagging and planarity checks, and loop nesting runs on a synthetic 8x8 lattice rather than the simulated/segmented dual faces." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.09e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-runions-leaf-venation-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law — Parameter expressivity: 40/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Runions Table 1 (15 parameter regimes) is vendored in venation_reference.json, but simulate_venation() hardcodes step_D, b_s, b_v, and d_k per mode without reading Table 1 or sweeping parameters. Evidence: 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py L215–L241: Hardcoded step_D, b_s, b_v, d_k in simulate_venation() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py#L215-L241>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
